{"term":"credit","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5b4033a487701f148e","definition":"To believe; to put credence in.","example":"Someone said there were over 100,000 people there, but I can't credit that.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["accept","believe"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d958d050aee6d1fa71","definition":"To add to an account.","example":"Credit accounts receivable with the amount of the invoice.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["debit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c797474a3dd757965a","definition":"To acknowledge the contribution of.","example":"I credit the town council with restoring the shopping district.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f065a026e5338c0b3","definition":"To bring honour or repute upon; to do credit to; to raise the estimation of.","example":"You credit the church as much by your government as you did the school formerly by your wit.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4c07b1843718275e00","definition":"Reliance on the truth of something said or done; faith; trust.","example":"When Jonathan and the people heard these words they gave no credit into them, nor received them.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:73a4b03ccc466ac0d9","definition":"Recognition, respect and admiration.","example":"I give you credit for owning up to your mistake.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["due"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1dc54335fcce7bf92a","definition":"Acknowledgement of a contribution, especially in the performing arts.","example":"She received a singing credit in last year's operetta.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f4d7ac4cad9b9a3c31","definition":"Written titles and other information about the TV program or movie shown at the beginning and/or end of the TV program or movie.","example":"They kissed, and then the credits rolled.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"plural-normally","register":"countable, plural-normally, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1ee1ec7160c42f3de2","definition":"A privilege of delayed payment extended to a buyer or borrower on the seller's or lender's belief that what is given will be repaid.","example":"In view of your payment record, we are happy to extend further credit to you.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a63ed0fd87b09c693b","definition":"The time given for payment for something sold on trust.","example":"a long credit or a short credit","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:edd214d4359892e575","definition":"A person's credit rating or creditworthiness, as represented by their history of borrowing and repayment (or non payment).","example":"What do you mean my credit is no good?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US","register":"US, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35d5702373db2d8801","definition":"An addition to certain accounts; the side of an account on which payments received are entered.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c60ca88b9e61abf3af","definition":"A reduction in taxes owed, or a refund for excess taxes paid.","example":"Didn't you know that the IRS will refund any excess payroll taxes that you paid if you use the 45(B) general business credit?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cca6c2ba6d87ed32ce","definition":"A source of value, distinction or honour.","example":"That engineer is a credit to the team.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2657d5092b1fb9ad3f","definition":"A unit of currency used in a fictional universe or timeframe.","example":"To repair your star cruiser will cost 100,000 credits.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:12a31150b1fa9f9047","definition":"A nominal unit of value assigned outside of a currency system.","example":"Would you like to play? I put in a dollar and I've got two credits left.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6907d67254e460f216","definition":"Recognition for having taken a course (class).","example":"If you do not come to class, you will not get credit for the class, regardless of how well you do on the final.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b94e1db641bbd33026","definition":"A course credit, a credit hour – used as measure if enough courses have been taken for graduation.","example":"Dude, I just need 3 more credits to graduate – I can take socio-linguistics of Swahili if I want.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["unit"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["discredit","miscredit","recredit","uncredit","credible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0c9f4420fbfd33814f","definition":"A surname.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],